  "screenshotPath": "/home/onnwee/.t3/userdata/browser-artifacts/browser-screenshot-duyucare-dops-agency-murejuec-71102953.png",
  "bodyText": " \n1\n \n1\n2\n8\n9\n0\n0\n1\n2\n3\n9\n1\n2\n3\n8\n9\n0\n%\n\nRESTORE YOUR\nTHYROID HEALTH\n\nSTART YOUR BEST\nGOOD HABIT\n\nScience\nOur Story\nCommunity\nPre-order Thyroid Hero®\nThe New Standard of Thyroid Health\nSCROLL\n\nThyroid Health is the north star to unlocking whole-body health. At Duyu Care we believe in creating health rather than fighting disease by developing scientifically-studied products that support your thyroid function and overall health.\n\nPre-Order\nYour Endocrine\n\n\nSystem, Optimised\nThyroid Hero®\n[01]\n\nYour thyroid is your body's silent hero, tirelessly working behind the scenes to keep your metabolism, energy levels, and mood in check.\n\n[02]\n\nThe thyroid gland requires several key nutrients for optimal function. These nutrients are essential for the production, conversion, and regulation of thyroid hormones.\n\n[03]\n\nOur nutritionist-formulated, full-spectrum supplement delivers these essential vitamins, minerals and adaptogens in one daily serving.\n\n[04]\n\nCaring for your thyroid made easy.\n\nImmune Function\n\nAntioxidant Defence\n\nMetabolic Function\n\nWeight Maintenance\n\nCognitive Function\n\nBalanced Energy, Reduced Fatigue + Brain Fog,\nMood + Stress Regulation\n\nMenstrual Health\n\nPeriod Regularity\nSymptom Relief\n\nSkin Health\n\nShinier Hair, Stronger Nails\nHydrated Skin\n\nThyroid Hero — Fitting seamlessly\ninto your daily routine. \nSay hello to thyroid\ncare that truly cares\nabout you.\nPre-Order Now\nABOUT US\nWe Share Your\nLived Experience\n\nIn November 2020, co-founders and partners Marie Peinert and Raphael Reuben discovered that Marie suffered from an autoimmune thyroid condition. Together, they embarked on the journey to recovery through holistic care. Like Marie, 800 million people worldwide are affected by thyroid conditions. Duyu Care exists to help those living with and managing these chronic conditions daily and provide best-in-class preventative care for everyone else.\n\nGet to know us\n\nThrough my personal health journey, I've come to realise that empowering individuals to take charge of their own health has the potential to revolutionise our approach to healthcare.\n\nMarie Peinert, Duyu Co-Founder & CEO\n\nWHY WE’RE DIFFERENT\nMODULE\n\n1\n2\n3\n4\n/\n4\n\nOur Reactive\nProactive Approach\n\nHealthcare, as it exists today, is often reactive, exclusively\nprescriptive, and only treats the symptoms — not the human.\n\nThe daily challenges of managing chronic stress, exposure to toxic\npollutants, inflammation, and nutrient-deficient diets are\nunavoidable. It's never too early to incorporate healthy habits\nbecause maintaining well-being requires a proactive, preventative\napproach.\n\nCare for Every\nBody\n\nWherever you are on your healing journey, we've got you. Duyu\nprovides holistic solutions that empower agency over your body\nand daily choices. In addition to providing science-backed\nsupplements to support your thyroid health, immune response, and\ndigestive function, we also offer on-demand testing for radically\nbetter understanding and personalised protocols to support your\nunique health goals.\n\nDaily Rituals\nPowered By Science\n\nWe care about the cold, hard facts. Duyu is your go-to health and\nwellness partner — we formulate a clean and potent Full-Spectrum\nThyroid Supplement made with 13 scientifically studied ingredients\nproven to support your thyroid, whole-body health, and day-to-day\nwell-being.\n\nGood Habits\nAre Cool\n\nHealth relies on our daily choices. Health is a verb. It's an active\npursuit. It's also self-defined. We want to live in a world where\nillness is optional — or at least — navigable or preventable due to\ndaily lifestyle choices such as diet, exercise (movement), mental\nhealth, sleep hygiene, and having a sense of community. Duyu is a\ncommunity that supports your preventative routines/ good-habit\nlifestyle.\n\nDid you know?\n\nOver 800 million people worldwide are affected by\n\nThyroid Conditions\nSCIENCE\nWhy our\napproach is\nimportant\n\nCitations\n\n1. \"Symptoms of Thyroid Problems.\" UPMC South Central Pennsylvania Endocrinology. Retrieved from https://www.upmc.com/services/south-central-pa/endocrinology/thyroid/symptoms\n2. \"The majority of thyroid patients still suffering years on from diagnosis\" (2023). University of Aberdeen. Retrieved from https://www.abdn.ac.uk/news/17040/\n3. Santos, L. R., Vasconcelos Bessa, I., Gaspar da Rocha, A., Neves, C., Freitas, C., & Soares, P. (2023). Survey on selenium clinical supplementation in autoimmune thyroid disease. European thyroid journal, 12(2), e220090. https://doi.org/10.1530/ETJ-22-0090\n\n0\n\nare undiagnosed\n\n0\n\nto get diagnosed\n\n0\n\nstill experience symptoms after receiving treatment\n\n0\n\nof physicians recommend supplementation as a daily part of thyroid treatment\n\nFAQ\nHave questions?\n[01]\n\nWhat are the 13 key ingredients in Thyroid HeroTM?\n\nAshwagandha, Organic Chaga, L-Tyrosine, Beta Carotene, Selenium, Vitamin D3, Vitamin B12, Vitamin B1, Vitamin B2, Iodine, Magnesium Glycinate, Zinc, and Iron.\n\n[02]\n\nWhat are the health benefits of each key ingredient?\n\nAshwagandha: An ancient medicinal herb and adaptogen that helps the body manage stress, normalise thyroid biomarkers, and alleviates brain fog.\nOrganic Chaga: Supports immune system regulation (reduced thyroid antibodies), reduced inflammation, and stress management that may affect the thyroid.\nL-Tyrosine: Supports thyroid hormone production and balance, and helps bolster stress response.\nBeta Carotene: Helps Vitamin A absorption in the body to support metabolic function, cellular reproduction, and retinol production.\nSelenium: A trace mineral critical to thyroid hormone metabolism and the antioxidant defense of the thyroid gland. Selenium is also an active immunomodulator (helps to regulate the immune system).\nVitamin D3: Helps restore the stem cells that seal and heal gaps in the gastrointestinal tract (leaky gut). Vitamin D helps to re-train T and B cell soldiers to regulate inflammation and antibodies attacking the thyroid.\nVitamin B12: Nearly 50% of people with Hypothyroidism and Hashimoto’s have a vitamin B12 deficiency. Vitamin B12 is required for proper red blood cell formation, cognitive function, and DNA synthesis.\nVitamin B1: Supports thyroid function (especially in those who experience an overactive thyroid).\nVitamin B2: Riboflavin is a water-soluble vitamin that the body uses to metabolize fats, protein, and carbohydrates into glucose for energy. Supports mood regulation (depression), migraine reduction, and helps calm many Hashimoto’s symptoms.\nIodine: Helps the thyroid gland produce Thyroxine which supports skeletal and nerve growth and metabolic function (absorption of proteins, fats, and carbohydrates in the body).\nMagnesium Glycinate: Helps regulate protein synthesis, muscle and nerve function, blood sugar, and blood pressure. Supports deep sleep, helps with migraines, and helps reduce blood pressure.\nZinc: A trace element required for the synthesis of thyroid hormones, and deficiency may result in Hypothyroidism.\nIron: Supports immune function, digestion, balanced energy, cognitive",
